WEEK–5: Synchronous and Asynchronous Kafka Producer

Aim: Implement sending messages both synchronously and asynchronously in a Kafka producer.

1. Start Kafka
docker-compose up -d

The Java producer must use 127.0.0.1:9093, because this is the host listener specified in the document.

2. AsyncProducer.java
package com.example.kafka;

import org.apache.kafka.clients.producer.*;
import org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer;
import java.util.*;

public class AsyncProducer {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
  Properties p=new Properties();
  p.put("bootstrap.servers","127.0.0.1:9093");
  p.put("key.serializer",StringSerializer.class.getName());
  p.put("value.serializer",StringSerializer.class.getName());

  KafkaProducer<String,String> producer=new KafkaProducer<>(p);

  for(int i=1;i<=5;i++)
   producer.send(new ProducerRecord<>("demo-topic",
    "async-key-"+i,"async-message-"+i),
    (m,e)->System.out.println("Sent async: "+m.offset()));

  producer.flush();

  for(int i=1;i<=5;i++)
   try {
    RecordMetadata m=producer.send(
     new ProducerRecord<>("demo-topic",
     "sync-key-"+i,"sync-message-"+i)).get();
    System.out.println("Sent sync: "+m.offset());
   } catch(Exception e){System.out.println("Failed");}

  producer.close();
  System.out.println("All messages sent successfully!");
 }
}

This demonstrates both asynchronous send() with callback and synchronous send().get(), as required by Week-5.

3. SyncProducer.java
package com.example.kafka;

import org.apache.kafka.clients.producer.*;
import org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer;
import java.util.*;

public class SyncProducer {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
  Properties p=new Properties();
  p.put("bootstrap.servers","127.0.0.1:9093");
  p.put("key.serializer",StringSerializer.class.getName());
  p.put("value.serializer",StringSerializer.class.getName());

  KafkaProducer<String,String> producer=new KafkaProducer<>(p);

  for(int i=1;i<=10;i++)
   try {
    RecordMetadata m=producer.send(
     new ProducerRecord<>("demo-topic",
     "sync-key-"+i,"sync-message-"+i)).get();
    System.out.println("Sent sync: "+m.offset());
   } catch(Exception e){System.out.println("Failed");}

  producer.close();
  System.out.println("All synchronous messages sent successfully!");
 }
}

This follows the document's separate synchronous producer, which sends 10 messages using blocking send().get().

4. Compile and Run

From the kafka-producer-demo folder:

mvn clean package

Run asynchronous producer:

java -jar target/kafka-producer-demo-1.0-SNAPSHOT-shaded.jar

Run synchronous producer:

java -cp target/kafka-producer-demo-1.0-SNAPSHOT-shaded.jar com.example.kafka.SyncProducer

